From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0263: ADSP QMI for sensor streams; the vibration motor

The ADSP's sensor client (SNS_CLIENT, QMI over QRTR node 5) is reached from
user space through /dev/redwood-qmi. The ADSP edge is now written safely from
both threads that use it: a lock for its GLINK TX FIFO and one for the send
queues and the ADSP's receive-buffer table; the queues hold 128 packets (32)
and drop the oldest when full, counted and logged. The services the ADSP
announces go into the QMI lookup table like the modem's.

The vibration motor, the PM7250B LDO vibrator (SPMI SID 3, 0x5300): new
bsd/dev/sweet_vibrate.c with kern.sweet_vibrate (on for N ms, at most 2000,
0 stops; a new request replaces the running one) and kern.sweet_vibrate_pattern
("on,off,on,..." ms, up to 10 steps). 3000 mV is set once, EN_CTL bit 7 turns
it on (VREG_READY polled, bounded) and a thread call turns it off; the first
vibration logs the registers. sweet_spmi_write also allows SID 3 0x53xx.
